+## Admin Escalation & Sandbox Approvals
+
+Security governance mandates that custom scripted fields run in the most restrictive sandbox possible. However, certain enterprise integrations and calculated fields require elevated capabilities, such as Tier B (`nsjail`) containerized execution needing outbound network egress or local filesystem access, or scripts querying data across workspace and server boundaries.
+
+These operations cannot execute under default project permissions and must pass through the **Admin Escalation & Security Approvals** lifecycle managed by `EscalationApprovalPanel`.
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+    autonumber
+    actor Dev as Project Developer / Admin
+    participant Panel as EscalationApprovalPanel (UI)
+    participant API as Custom Fields API (/api/v1)
+    participant Approver as Distinct Tier Approver (AAL2)
+    participant Sandbox as Tier B Sandbox (nsjail)
+
+    Dev->>Panel: Define Tier B script needing egress / filesystem access
+    Dev->>Panel: Submit Escalation Request with justification
+    Panel->>API: POST /approvals (records manifest SHA-256, status: PENDING)
+    Note over Panel,Approver: Dual-Control & Scope Matrix Evaluation
+    Approver->>Panel: Inspect blast radius, manifest digest & justification
+    Approver->>Panel: Verify Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) step-up
+    Approver->>API: POST /approvals/:id/approve (signs SHA-256 digest)
+    API-->>Sandbox: Authorize time-bounded execution token with nsjail flags
+    Note over Panel,Sandbox: Script tampering auto-revokes approval immediately
+```
+
+### The Approval Lifecycle
+
+Every privilege escalation follows a deterministic state machine:
+
+1. **`Default` (No Approval Needed):** Standard Tier A (Wasmtime) fields running with default Project scope and Invoking User credentials run without administrative escalation.
+2. **`Pending Approval`:** When elevated scope (`WORKSPACE`, `SERVER`) or elevated credentials (`PROJECT_ADMIN_SP`, `SERVER_ADMIN_SP`) are requested, the field transitions to `PENDING`. Execution is blocked until an authorized administrator reviews the request.
+3. **`Pending Second Approver`:** High-impact configurations (such as Server-wide scope or Server Admin service-principals) enforce multi-party authorization. The request requires approval from a second distinct administrator before activation.
+4. **`Approved`:** Once an administrator holding the required authority tier verifies their AAL2 credentials, signs the manifest SHA-256 hash, and acknowledges any elevated service-principal warnings, the field is activated.
+5. **`Revoked`:** If any administrator or developer alters the script source code, configuration schema, or target scope, the manifest SHA-256 digest no longer matches. The system immediately auto-revokes approval, reverting status to `REVOKED` and halting execution until re-approved.
+
+### Cryptographic Signature & Integrity Requirements
+
+To prevent privilege escalation via database manipulation or unauthorized script mutation:
+
+- **Manifest SHA-256 Binding:** Every approval request is cryptographically bound to the SHA-256 digest of the script source and field definition (`manifest_sha256`). Approval applies strictly to that exact binary hash.
+- **AAL2 Re-Authentication:** Approvers cannot rely on existing session cookies alone. Approving an escalation triggers an interactive WebSudo AAL2 challenge requiring WebAuthn/Passkey or TOTP re-authentication.
+- **Anti-Tamper Auto-Revocation:** At runtime, the sandbox dispatcher re-computes the script SHA-256 hash before container invocation. If a discrepancy is detected between the database record and the approved signature, execution aborts with a `MANIFEST_MISMATCH` alert.
+- **Audit Ledger Logging:** All approval requests, reviews, approvals, and auto-revocations are recorded in the immutable audit ledger with administrator identity, timestamp, IP address, and SHA-256 digest.
+
+### Tier B (`nsjail`) Network and Filesystem Policies
+
+Tier B scripts run in hardened Linux namespaces (`CLONE_NEWPID`, `CLONE_NEWNET`, `CLONE_NEWNS`). When an escalation is approved:
+
+| Sandbox Capability | Default Execution | Approved Escalated Execution |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| **Network Egress** | Disabled (`CLONE_NEWNET`) | Explicit allowlisted egress proxies with mTLS authentication |
+| **Filesystem Access** | Read-only root mount | Isolated ephemeral scratch mount (`/tmp`) cryptographically shredded on completion |
+| **Credential Mode** | Invoking user token | Project Admin Service Principal or Server Admin Service Principal (Dual-Control) |
+| **Target Scope** | Project-only metadata | Workspace or Server metadata with rate-limiting and audit tracking |
+
